"The biconditional statement that we proved in Logical Equivalence World were easy -- they could all be handled by substitution (i.e. the §0 tactic). But, in general, the proof of the **forward** direction of a biconditional (that being §1) can look ***a lot*** different than the proof of the **backward** direction of a biconditional (that being §2)."
