#. §0: `∧`
#. §1: $$ (P ∧ Q) ↔ (Q ∧ P) $$
#. §2: `And_comm`
#. §3: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|cc||cc|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & P ∧ Q & Q ∧ P  \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T & T \\
#.   T & F & F & F \\
#.   F & T & F & F \\
#.   F & F & F & F \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
msgid "This is the **Commutative Law** for §0. It says that\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"The proof of §2 follows from the truth-table below:\n"
"§3"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `obtain`
#. §1: `obtain`
#. §2: ```
#. obtain hQ := hPQ (hP)
#. ```
#. §3: `hPQ`
#. §4: `hP`
#. §5: ```
#. obtain hQ := hPQ hP
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L01_arg
msgid "### **❯ The §0 tactic**\n"
"The §1 tactic allows us to introduce new assumptions into our current proof *as long as* we supply proofs (in the current context) of those assumptions. 👉 Try the following basic usage:\n"
"§2\n"
"**Note:** the space between §3 (the *function*) and §4 (the *input*). Since the argument here is *atomic*, the parentheses are optional. So even the following ought to work:\n"
"§5\n"
""
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.PfWorld.L12_pf
msgid "Great. We can clear this subgoal in one line."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|cc||c||cc||c|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & P → Q & ¬ Q & ¬ P & ¬ Q → ¬ P  \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T & F & F & T \\
#.   T & F & F & T & F & F \\
#.   F & T & T & F & T & T \\
#.   F & F & T & T & T & T \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
msgid "An implication is logically equivalent to its contrapositive. We can prove this via a truth-table:\n"
"§0"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $$ ¬ (P ∧ Q) ↔ (¬ P ∨ ¬ Q)$$
#. §1: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|cc||c||cc||c|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & ¬ (P ∧ Q) & ¬ P & ¬ Q & ¬ P ∨ ¬ Q  \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & F & F & F & F \\
#.   T & F & T & F & T & T \\
#.   F & T & T & T & F & T \\
#.   F & F & T & T & T & T \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.EquivWorld_eg.equiv_eg_docs
msgid "This is half of **DeMorgan's Law**. It says that\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"We can prove DeMorgan's Law with a truth-table:\n"
"§1"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h : P ∧ Q`
#. §1: ```
#. obtain hP : = h.left
#. ```
#. §2: `hP : P`
#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L04_arg
msgid "We simply need to destructure the assumption §0. 👉 Try:\n"
"§1\n"
"This will create a new assumption, namely §2.\n"
""
msgstr ""

#. §0: $$ P ∨ P ↔ P $$
#. §1: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|c||c|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & P ∨ P \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T \\
#.   F & T & F \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.EquivWorld_eg.equiv_eg_docs
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.EquivWorld_eg.equiv_eg_docs
msgid "This is an **Idempotent Law**. It says that\n"
"\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"We can prove the **Idempotent Law** with a truth-table:\n"
"§1"
msgstr ""

#. §0: ```
#. (∀ x, P x) ∧ (∀ x, Q x) ↔ ∀ x, P x ∧ Q x
#. ```
#. §1: `Forall_and`
#: Game.Levels.QuantifierWorld.L07_quant
msgid "The converse of this is also true. From here on out the logical equivalence\n"
"§0\n"
"is available and called §1."
